## Verification Explanation

Define the submission interface, metric, correctness/performance gates and
failure behavior consistently with raw-instruction.md and instruction.md.
The separate verifier combines the task metric with a trajectory integrity audit.

### Budgets and resources

The primary grader supervisor has @@GRADER_TIMEOUT@@ seconds. Document its
candidate build/query/training budgets, repeats and cleanup so they fit this
window. The trajectory session has @@JUDGE_TIMEOUT@@ seconds; its wrapper has
@@JUDGE_SUPERVISOR_TIMEOUT@@ seconds. The outer verifier includes a further
600 seconds for setup, finalization and cleanup, totaling @@VERIFIER_TIMEOUT@@ seconds.
Choose resource limits from the workload and validate their enforcement.

### Local validation

Configure coding-agent credentials and verifier-only `VERIFIER_OPENAI_BASE_URL`
(`https://openrouter.ai/api/v1`) and `VERIFIER_OPENAI_API_KEY` in an ignored local
`.env`. Submission APIs, if supplied, have separate documented credentials.
The trajectory judge uses RewardKit 0.2.0 and
`deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash`; adapt its rubric to this task.

```bash
python scripts/check_tasks.py tasks/@@TASK_NAME@@
python scripts/download_assets.py --task @@TASK_NAME@@ --verify-only
bash scripts/run_task.sh --task @@TASK_NAME@@ --agent codex --openrouter \
  --model YOUR_MODEL --reasoning-effort YOUR_SUPPORTED_EFFORT --dry-run
```

Restore actual inputs, test the grader and replace placeholders before running
the configured model. For GPU runs, add `--gpu-device <host-index-or-UUID>`.
Record commands, results, model feedback and final revision in [VALIDATION.md](VALIDATION.md).

